235. Construct a circle,

a) passing through two given points $A$ and $B$, intersecting a given circle (or line) $S$ at a known angle $a$;

b) passing through a given point $A$, intersecting two given circles (or two lines, or a line and a circle) $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ at known angles $\alpha$ and $\beta$.

8.89. Given angle $A O B$. Construct:

a) an angle twice as large as angle $A O B$;

b) an angle half as large as angle $A O B$.
